23 0 obj
<< /A 617 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating the selection and allocation of pediatric AML patients for chemotherapy cycles prior to hematopoietic cell transplantation, including numbers excluded, group assignments, MRD status after cycles, and analytical inclusion criteria.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 15 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 618 0 R /Alt (Kaplan-Meier survival plot comparing relapse-free survival rates over two years after hematopoietic cell transplantation \(HCT\) for two groups: one with one to two chemotherapy cycles and another with three to four cycles. Both groups show similar trends in relapse-free survival, with overlapping confidence intervals and a p-value of zero point eight four, indicating no significant difference. Tables below the plot display numbers at risk, cumulative events, and survival percentages with confidence intervals at baseline, one year, and two years.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 18 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 619 0 R /Alt (Line graph comparing cumulative incidence of relapse after hematopoietic cell transplantation over two years for patients receiving one to two cycles \(black line\) versus three to four cycles \(gray line\) of treatment, showing higher relapse in the three to four cycle group with a non-significant p-value of zero point two three; includes risk numbers, cumulative events, and confidence intervals beneath the graph.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 19 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 620 0 R /Alt (Kaplan-Meier survival plot comparing overall survival after hematopoietic cell transplantation between patients receiving 1 to 2 cycles versus 3 to 4 cycles, with survival curves, number at risk, cumulative events, confidence intervals, and p-value of zero point four six displayed.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 19 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
27 0 obj
<< /A 621 0 R /Alt (Line graph showing non-relapse mortality \(NRM\) cumulative incidence by years after HCT, comparing patients receiving one to two cycles versus three to four cycles. The one to two cycles group shows an increase in NRM incidence to 18 percent at one year, while the three to four cycles group remains at zero percent. Below the graph, risk tables present numbers at risk and cumulative events for each group. The p-value is 0.06.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 20 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
